{title: Mercy and Grace}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: C}
{tempo: 117}

Verse 1
[C]From the beginning of time was a plan
That all [F]who believe understand:
Salvation [C]is ours as a gift, through God's [Am7]only [G]Son.
[F]Leaving [C]Your glory on high,
[D7]Coming [F]to suffer and die,
Rising [C]again from the grave, the battle You [G]won!

Chorus
Saved by Your grace,
Freed by Your [C]mercy.
Saved by Your [G]grace,
Freed by [Em7]Your [C]mercy.
No more must I [F]do,
[Am7]No [Dm7]more can [D]I [G]say...
It is enough [F]that You, my Lord,
Died in my [G]place
[G7]Such mercy and [C]grace!

Bridge
[G]Now by [Am]Your Name I am known
Given [F]a heavenly home
[Fmaj7]Resting [Dm]secure in the [F]grace that has freed me from [C]sin.
Mercy, [Am]like [A]rain from above
[Am]Showered [F]upon me in love...
[C]Now [D]in Your mercy [Dm]and [F]grace, I'm rejoicing again...
Rejoicing [A#]again!

Verse 2
[G]Bearing [C]the burden of sin
And [F]needing a heavenly Friend,
[F]I [C]learned of Your mercy and grace
In Your holy [G]Word.
[F]Life [C]everlasting and free:
This [F]is Your promise to me...
[Fmaj7]Words [C]more amazing and true, I never have [G]heard!
[G]{c: [C]Repeat chorus}
Saved by Your grace,
[B]Freed [G]by Your mercy.
[G]Saved by Your grace,
[A]Freed [G]by Your mercy.
[C]No more must I [F]do,
[Am7]No [D]more can I [G]say...
It is [F]enough that You, my Lord,
Died in my [G]place
Such mercy and [C]grace!
